.TH HTTP_READ_HEADER 3
.SH NAME
http_read_header \- read the headers of a response from a buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "ssize_t http_read_header(buffer* " in ", stralloc* " out ", http_response* " response ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_read_header ()
reads header lines from
.I in
and appends them to
.IR out
while the status of
.I response
is HTTP_RECV_HEADER. It takes the status code from the status line, selects
.I transfer
from Content-Length (and sets
.IR content_length ),
Transfer-Encoding: chunked or a multipart Content-Type (and sets the
.IR boundary ),
and at the empty line sets
.I headers_len
and the status HTTP_RECV_DATA.
.P
This belongs to the first reader of the module, written for
.BR buffer (3)
operations; it expects
.I h->stream
to be cleared. New code should use
.BR http_recv (3).
.SH RETURN VALUE
The result of the last line read: greater than 0 while lines are parsed, 0 or less when the buffer holds no complete line, which is not an error for a non-blocking socket.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_canread(3), http_read_internal(3)
